# A source files use the .a extension, which GitHub Linguist does not know;
# without an override it falls back to content heuristics and reports them
# as C. Linguist only resolves linguist-language to languages in its
# languages.yml (custom names are not supported), so "A" is not a valid
# value. Until A is added to Linguist upstream, mark .a files with an
# unknown language name: they are then excluded from the language stats
# instead of being misreported. Remove this line once Linguist ships "A".
*.a linguist-language=A
